course: dictionary
lesson: 10411
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The clues around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. Trill is a good example: it can be a bird's sound, a musical ornament, a speech sound, or a way of talking.
explain: «Warm-ups such as lip trills and humming help the breath and the voice muscles work without strain.» Warm-ups tells you singers are practising, so a lip trill must be a quick, repeated sound made with the voice, not a bird's song.
explain: Ask yourself what the topic is. Birds mean a bird's song, music means quick notes, and language means a rolled sound. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Trill means a quick, high, repeated sound, like a bird singing.
fact: In music, a trill is two neighbouring notes played or sung very quickly, one after the other, many times.
fact: In language, a trill is a sound made by letting the tongue flutter, like the rolled «r» in Spanish.
fact: To trill is to make such a sound, or to say something in a high, happy voice.
fact: «Warm-ups such as lip trills and humming help the breath and the voice muscles work without strain.» Here a lip trill is made by blowing through loose lips.
exercise: «The robin began to trill from the top of the hedge.» What does trill mean here? | A slow, deep growl | *A quick, high, repeated sound | A loud crash | A kind of sweet cake
exercise: «Singers warm up with humming and lip trills so the voice works without strain.» What is a lip trill? | A song sung with no notes at all | A type of biscuit eaten after a concert | A loud drum beat | *A quick, repeated buzz made by blowing through loose lips
exercise: In music, what is a trill? | A song sung without any words | *Two neighbouring notes played very quickly, one after the other, many times | A loud drum beat | One note held for a long time
test: «She let her tongue trill on the r, the way Spanish speakers do.» Which meaning of trill is this? | A piano lesson | A bird's song from a tree | A loud cry for help | *A sound made by letting the tongue flutter
test: «"Good morning!" trilled the cheerful girl.» What does trilled mean here? | Shouted in anger | *Said in a high, happy voice | Whispered in a secret voice | Fell asleep in the chair
exam: Pick the best meaning of trill in «The lark began to trill over the meadow.» | Fall into a deep sleep | *Make a quick, high, repeated sound | Hit a drum very hard | Stop moving completely
